    "long_instructions": "## Debug the Fitness Tracker\r\n\r\n1. Click each button and observe how the tracker’s state changes.\r\n2. Compare what happens to what the hints say *should* happen.\r\n3. Find bugs where the state:\r\n   - doesn’t change  \r\n   - changes the wrong way  \r\n   - resets  \r\n   - behaves strangely  \r\n   - shows the wrong value  \r\n4. Record each bug in `documentation.md`.\r\n5. Fix the code in `script.js` and test again.\r\n\r\n<br/>\r\n\r\n:::details [Not Sure Where to Start?]\r\nIf you’re not sure where something is in the code or how it works, use AI Tutor to ask questions like:\r\n- “Where is the steps value stored?”\r\n- “Why doesn’t this value change when I click the button?”\r\n- “What happens when I add a number to a string?”\r\n:::",
